% ============================================================================
% opposites.query.adj — a worked recall over the word-opposites library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what is the opposite of
% hot?": it states no fact of its own — it only `import`s the grounded table and
% asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against the `opposite` rows
% and returns EVERY opposite + the table's source/locator/trust (as of this
% cycle's extension, a bound word can recall MULTIPLE opposites — `happy` now
% recalls sad ; blue ; depressed ; ... ; unhappy, not just one). A word the
% table does not carry abstains honestly — the engine never invents an
% opposite.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli opposites.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "opposites.adj"

? opposite(hot, $Word)         % expect cold ; chilled
? opposite(happy, $Word)       % expect sad ; blue ; depressed ; down ; miserable ; moody ; morose ; unhappy
? opposite(big, $Word)         % expect small ; little ; tiny ; minuscule ; miniature ; minute (added this cycle)
? opposite(purple, $Word)      % expect abstain — no opposite is shipped for purple
